[[Selachimorpha]] is a [[Legendary equipment|legendary]] piece of [[Aquatic Headgear]] contained in the [[Selachimorpha Container]] which unlocks all the armor weights, added with ''[[Guild Wars 2: Visions of Eternity|Visions of Eternity]]''.

== Lore ==
{{legendary unlock text|"Thought I was pullin' yer fins, didn't ya? I told ya. I tell... I tell no... I told ya the truth!" —[["Captain" Ruymond Lakes|"Captain" Lakes]]|icon=Selachimorpha.png}}

[[Agaleus]] is an artifact of the Spirit of the Wild [[Shark (Spirit of the Wild)|Shark]] and greatly improves its wearer's swimming capabilities, giving them some of the physical features of a shark. [[Captain Weyandt]], known as a collector of valuable and powerful items, acquired the pieces of Agaleus with the help of one of his crew members who was a former Shaman of Shark. Weyandt, fearing mutiny, decided to hide the pieces of the mask where he alone would be able to retrieve them. He hid the pieces in the waters of [[Shipwreck Strand]], [[Siren's Reef]], [[Southsun Cove]], [[Lion's Arch]], [[Bloodtide Coast]] and [[Cursed Shore]], but some of the pieces ended up in the possession of [[Captain Wiley]] and [[Admiral Taidha Covington]].

Agaleus would eventually be reassembled by the same former Shaman of Shark who originally found the pieces, but only after the new recipient of the mask proved themselves to Shark by helping the Spirit in [[Honor of the Waves]].

